On Mon, Dec 21, 2026 at 9:12 AM Mateo Alvarez <mateo@redwood.com> wrote:
> Quick summary and proposed plan for the SDK onboarding window this week...

Hi team — answering Sandeep's bullets and dropping in concise sample snippets below.

Retries: client-side only is the safest approach for your pattern. Recommend: client retries for idempotent calls only (GETs/embeddings) and 3 attempts with exponential backoff (150ms, 450ms, 1.35s). For POSTs that create state, rely on idempotency keys + 1 retry max. Redwood's gateway will not automatically retry POSTs for your sandbox unless you opt into the gateway-level retry policy in the MAP.

Ramp: 600 req/min is aggregated across the app cluster. With 2 instances, start at 300 req/min per instance and step up every 4 hours (300 -> 450 -> 600).

Warmup success criteria (we'll monitor together):
- p95 latency < 120ms for generation endpoints during steady-state
- 5xx rate < 0.5% sustained over 15 minutes
- KV/cache hit ratio stabilizes above 60% for repeated prefixes (if you enable prefix caching)

Inline sample (Node) — simple request with recommended timeouts/retries: 
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
async function invoke(payload, apiKey) {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timeout = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 10000); // 10s
  try {
    // basic exponential retry loop for idempotent calls
    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
      try {
        const res = await fetch('https://sandbox.redwood-inference.net/v1/sdkgateway/generate', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
          signal: controller.signal
        });
        if (res.ok) return await res.json();
        if (res.status >= 500) throw new Error('server');
        // for 429, optionally backoff based on Retry-After header
      } catch (e) {
        if (attempt === 2) throw e;
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 150 * Math.pow(3, attempt)));
      }
    }
  } finally { clearTimeout(timeout); }
}

Also attached is a tiny checklist (in the MAP):
- Confirm API key + whitelist CIDR
- Import sample app and run ./start-local.sh with NODE_ENV=sandbox
- Turn on Redwood SDK telemetry (env var REDWOOD_TELEMETRY=1) for the first 24h

I can present these snippets during the pairing session and walk through the telemetry dashboard.

